<article class="env-corollary" id="058L">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/058L">Corollary <span data-tag="058L">4.7.6.18</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $n \geq 0$ be an integer. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is locally $(n-2)$-truncated. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The tautological map $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{cosk}_{n}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ is a trivial Kan fibration. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(3)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The tautological map $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{cosk}_{n}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(4)$</dt>
<dd><p>
There exists an $n$-coskeletal $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ which is equivalent to $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      The equivalence $(1) \Leftrightarrow (2)$ follows from Proposition <a data-tag="06RM" href="/tag/06RM">4.7.6.15</a>, the implication $(2) \Rightarrow (3)$ from Corollaries <a data-tag="06RP" href="/tag/06RP">4.7.6.17</a> and <a data-tag="01EH" href="/tag/01EH">4.5.4.12</a> the implication $(3) \Rightarrow (4)$ is trivial, and the implication $(4) \Rightarrow (1)$ follows from Corollary <a data-tag="06RN" href="/tag/06RN">4.7.6.16</a> and Remark <a data-tag="0586" href="/tag/0586">4.7.6.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
